# ================================
#  GLOBAL WORKSPACE RULES
# ================================

You are generating code for a large, multi-tenant SaaS system called TAKA.
All instructions in this workspace must follow these rules:

================================
1. CORE PRINCIPLES
================================

- Always respect the architecture and requirements described in `/docs/spec.md`.
- Before coding any module, always read the spec and confirm understanding.
- Work in small, atomic steps. Do NOT generate large patches unless explicitly asked.
- Always show a clear diff preview before applying changes.
- If something is unclear, ALWAYS ask clarifying questions.
- Never invent endpoints, fields, or models not documented in the spec unless asked to.
- Never refactor unrelated code unless explicitly instructed.

================================
2. TECH STACK RULES
================================
You must use the following stack:

Backend:
- Next.js 15 (App Router)
- TypeScript
- Prisma ORM
- PostgreSQL (Supabase)
- Supabase Auth
- tRPC (preferred) or REST ONLY if requested
- Zod validation

Frontend:
- React (inside Next.js)
- TailwindCSS
- Shadcn UI components
- Zustand or Context for local state
- React Query if needed
- Responsive-first design

Payments:
- Stripe or Paysera (implement Stripe first unless told otherwise)

Storage:
- Supabase Storage for all images

================================
3. FILE & FOLDER STRUCTURE RULES
================================
Use this structure:

/
 ├─ app/
 │   ├─ (public-facing pages)
 │   ├─ dashboard/
 │   ├─ api/
 │   ├─ auth/
 ├─ components/
 ├─ styles/
 ├─ lib/
 │   ├─ auth/
 │   ├─ db/
 │   ├─ tenants/
 │   ├─ utils/
 ├─ prisma/
 │   ├─ schema.prisma
 ├─ docs/
 │   ├─ spec.md
 ├─ emails/
 ├─ public/
 └─ package.json

Rules:
- Never create new folders unless necessary.
- Never put API code inside random folders — use `app/api/**`.
- Landing builder UI lives in `/app/dashboard/landing-builder/**`.

================================
4. CODING STYLE RULES
================================
- Use TypeScript strict mode.
- Use named exports, NOT default exports (unless React components).
- Write clean, readable, documented code.
- Use async/await ONLY (no .then chains).
- Always use try/catch in server-side functions.
- Validate all input with Zod.
- NEVER hardcode URLs — use environment variables.

================================
5. MULTI-TENANCY RULES
================================
- Every database query MUST filter by tenantId unless superadmin.
- All new tables MUST include tenantId field.
- tenantId is extracted from session / JWT.
- Superadmin bypass is allowed only when explicitly requested.

================================
6. PRISMA RULES
================================
- Always run schema updates incrementally.
- NO automatic rewrites of existing models without confirmation.
- Always show a migration plan before applying.

================================
7. API RULES
================================
- Prefer tRPC for internal authenticated actions.
- Public endpoints must include rate limiting.
- All API calls must validate:
  - authentication
  - authorization (role)
  - tenantId
  - input schema

================================
8. UI RULES
================================
- Use Shadcn components.
- Use consistent Tailwind spacing.
- All UI must be mobile-responsive.
- Avoid inline styles.
- Use functional components.
- Use server actions only where appropriate.

================================
9. LANDING BUILDER RULES
================================
- Landing blocks must be modular and isolated.
- DO NOT mix block types in same code file.
- Use JSON schema for block definitions.
- Ensure each block can be added/removed/reordered.
- Allow mobile/desktop visibility settings.

================================
10. CONTACT FORM RULES
================================
- Forms must be fully dynamic based on DB-configured fields.
- Validation must match the admin-defined rules.
- Embeddable mode must be iframe-safe.

================================
11. PAYMENT RULES
================================
- Use secure Stripe flows.
- Webhooks must validate signature.
- Never mark payments as "paid" manually unless in dev mode.

================================
12. ANALYTICS RULES
================================
- Track events ONLY in allowed endpoints.
- Do NOT send PII to analytics.
- Conversion funnels must be clean and isolated.

================================
13. EMAIL RULES
================================
- Use email templates stored in `/emails`.
- Reminders must respect admin timing settings.
- Logs must be recorded for every sent email.

================================
14. SAFETY & CONSENT RULES
================================
- Always generate unique consent URLs.
- Never delete consents.
- Store time, IP, email, user agent.

================================
15. SUPERADMIN RULES
================================
- Superadmin must not see tenant passwords or sensitive auth data.
- Superadmin may override landing pages, but MUST log changes.

================================
16. COMMUNICATION RULES
================================
- Before starting any module, summarize the work plan.
- After completing any module, summarize what was done.
- For any action involving several files, ask for confirmation.

================================
17. CHANGE CONTROL RULES
================================
- Never modify core structure without explicit approval.
- Never rename folders without approval.
- Never introduce new dependencies silently.

================================
END OF WORKSPACE RULES
================================
